          "distinct": true,
          "id": "a57b4ede9303a0c024c51ded9ae0e2606b1b163f",
          "message": "feat(gui): OS-reported disk-usage probe for the status bar gauge (sq-cno90) [OPUS-4.8] (#1270)\n\nThe status bar disk gauge (sq-vw3ax, #820) reads the snapshot-bytes ESTIMATE —\nthe UTF-8 length of the persisted whole-dataset N-Quads snapshot. That is honest\nbut omits the workspace index JSON + encoding overhead the on-disk\n`$APPLOCALDATA/workspaces/*.json` files carry.\n\nThis adds the precise OS-reported figure:\n\n- `gui/src-tauri/src/disk.rs`: a `disk_usage` Tauri command that resolves\n  `$APPLOCALDATA/workspaces` (the same base dir the fs capability + workspace\n  store key off) and returns its REAL byte total via `dir_size_bytes` — a\n  recursive `stat()` walk that sums each regular file's `metadata.len()`. It\n  follows no symlink out of the tree (least-privilege: cannot escape / loop),\n  skips unreadable entries rather than panicking, and reports a missing dir as\n  `bytes: 0, exists: false` (an honest fresh-install answer, never fabricated).\n- The matching least-privilege capability note: `disk_usage` is an app-defined\n  command invocable by `core:default`; it adds NO new fs-plugin surface (reads\n  via the engine's own std::fs, confined in Rust to the workspaces subtree).\n- `tauri-ipc.ts` `nativeDiskUsage()` + engine-context `diskBytes` / `refreshDiskUsage`:\n  feature-detect the Tauri API, probe on mount + after each persisted import.\n- The status bar PREFERS the OS figure in the desktop shell (`disk N`) and FALLS\n  BACK to the estimate on the web target (`≈disk N`) — labelled which it is.\n\nHonest: the gauge goes from estimate to OS-reported in the DESKTOP shell only;\non the web target it stays the snapshot estimate. No fabricated figure either way.\n\nGates (both feature states — default + `hdt`): cargo build, clippy --all-targets\n-D warnings, cargo test (incl. 5 direct unit tests for the byte-summing walk:\nnested-dir sum, single file, empty dir, missing path, symlink-not-followed); MSRV\n`cargo +1.88 check`; gui/app typecheck + lint + build:tauri. The byte-summing walk\nis unit-tested directly. Cites #820.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
